here's a hard probability question  Lindsay randomly selects two distinct  days each week to go to the gym just  randomly selects three distinct days  each week to go to the same gym what is  the probability that Lindsay and Jess  will both be at the gym on the same day  at least once in any given week express  your answer as a common fraction  so we want the probability that they  will meet in the gym at least once in  any given week it'll be easier to  calculate the probability they do not  meet and then take one minus that  Lindsay randomly selects two distinct  days there are seven days in the week  and let's say Lindsay takes these two  days now Jess randomly selects three of  the days so the probability they do not  meet is if Jess selects three of the  days from the five days that Lindsay  does not go so this probability will be  equal to five choose 3 divided by the  total number of ways which is seven  choose three this simplifies to be two  over seven so probability they do meet  is one minus two over seven which gives  the answer 5 over 7.
 

